 "issue_title": "Bug: preserve row count when writing zero-column frames to Parquet",
 "issue_body": "## Summary\n`write_parquet()` silently loses row count when exporting an `ArFrame` that has rows but no columns.\n\n## Why it matters\nZero-column frames can be produced by column-selection or drop-column workflows. If such a frame has a meaningful row count, exporting it to Parquet should either preserve that row count or raise a clear unsupported-case error. Writing a file that reads back as zero rows can hide data-shape bugs in downstream validation or pipeline smoke tests.\n\n## Evidence\n- `arnio/io.py`: `write_parquet()` converts the frame with `to_pandas(frame)` and then calls `DataFrame.to_parquet(...)`.\n- `arnio/convert.py`: `to_pandas()` correctly creates `pd.DataFrame(index=pd.RangeIndex(cpp_frame.num_rows()))` when the frame has zero columns.\n- With pandas/pyarrow, writing a zero-column `DataFrame` with a default `RangeIndex` reads back as an empty `(0, 0)` DataFrame, so the original row count is lost.\n\n## Reproduction or trigger\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\nimport arnio as ar\n\nframe = ar.from_pandas(pd.DataFrame(index=range(3)))\nprint(frame.shape)\n# (3, 0)\n\nar.write_parquet(frame, \"zero_columns.parquet\")\nroundtrip = pd.read_parquet(\"zero_columns.parquet\")\nprint(roundtrip.shape)\n# Actual today: (0, 0)\n```\n\n## Expected behavior\n`write_parquet()` should either preserve the three-row shape when the file is read back, or explicitly reject non-empty zero-column frames with a clear `ValueError` explaining that this shape is not representable by the current Parquet export path.\n\n## Actual behavior\nThe export succeeds, but reading the Parquet file back returns `(0, 0)`, silently dropping the original row count.\n\n## Suggested direction\nAdd a focused guard in `write_parquet()` for zero-column frames with rows. Either:\n\n- preserve row count using an explicit metadata/index strategy that round-trips through pyarrow/pandas, or\n- reject the case clearly until row-count preservation is supported.\n\nAdd regression tests for:\n\n- `(0, 0)` empty frames\n- `(n, 0)` frames where `n > 0`\n- normal non-empty frames to confirm existing behavior is unchanged\n\n## References\n- `arnio/io.py`\n- `arnio/convert.py`\n- Related but separate: #1648 tracks zero-column row-count preservation for `to_arrow()`.",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/im-anishraj/arnio/issues/1942",
 "pr": 2007,
 "pr_title": "fix: reject zero-column Parquet export that drops row count",
 "pr_body": "\r\nFixes #1942\r\n\r\n## Summary\r\n- Add a guard in `write_parquet()` for `(n, 0)` frames where `n > 0`\r\n- Keep `(0, 0)` export behavior unchanged\r\n- Add regression tests for `(0, 0)`, `(n, 0)`, and normal frames\r\n\r\n## Test plan\r\n- [x] `pytest tests/test_parquet.py -v`\r\n- [x] `make test`\r\n- [x] `make lint`",
